---
term: Asset
section: jurisdiction-and-resources
order: 40
definition: Property or a resource that a corporation holds under its charter.
seeAlso:
  - ownership
  - dissolution
---
Assets enter a corporation through contributions, transfers, transactions, and acquisitions. They leave through transfers, sales, and relinquishment. Contributed assets become part of the corporation's [[commons]] and part of the basis for its [[jurisdiction]].
